<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-mkt soft wheat, barley.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-mkt soft wheat, barley.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following licences to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, a European grain industry source said.</p>
<p>There was no immediate official confirmation of the awards.</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Maximum rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  238,000		16.40 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley		138,500		27.49 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>EU member country officials later confirmed the wheat and barley awards, saying the EU also granted 10,000 tonnes of Greek maize at a maximum rebate of 36.88 Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>The EU's grain panel rejected all bids to export free-market durum wheat, rye and oats, they said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
